  "guide.page1": "A small pottery workshop\n\nClay becomes pottery clay, the wheel shapes it, the kiln fires it, and glaze is fired a second time.",
  "guide.page2": "Pottery clay\n\nCraft one clay ball and one sand for two natural clay. Add raw iron, iron nugget, raw copper, lapis lazuli, amethyst shard, or charcoal while mixing to make colored clay.",
  "guide.page3": "The pottery wheel\n\nUse an empty hand to cycle through storage jar, planter, and flower vase. Use pottery clay on the wheel and wait for the blank to form.",
  "guide.page4": "First firing\n\nAdd coal or charcoal to the kiln, then insert an unfired vessel. Wait for the bisque-fired piece to appear.",
  "guide.page5": "Glaze and fire again\n\nCombine a bisque-fired vessel with its matching glaze in the crafting grid. Fuel the kiln and fire the glaze-coated piece a second time.",
  "guide.page6": "Materials and recipes\n\nA guide can be remade with one clay ball and one paper. Colorants are simplified game recipes inspired by mineral pigments, not exact ceramic formulas."
}
